Update Hostname of Linux
============================

============================================================
           INSTRUCTIONS: CHANGE SLES HOSTNAME
============================================================

1. CHECK CURRENT HOSTNAME
   Run this command to see your current setup:
   $ hostnamectl

2. SET NEW HOSTNAME
   Apply your new name instantly and permanently:
   $ sudo hostnamectl set-hostname your-new-hostname
   
   *(Replace "your-new-hostname" with your actual name)*

3. UPDATE THE HOSTS FILE
   Open the configuration file in a text editor:
   $ sudo vi /etc/hosts
   
   -> Find any instances of your old hostname.
   -> Replace them with your new hostname.
   -> Save and exit the file.

4. VERIFY THE CHANGES
   Confirm the network system accepted the update:
   $ hostnamectl

============================================================
